{"source":"github","project_id":"gt-extras","target":"posit-dev/gt-extras","id":"pr/170","ref":170,"title":"Replace scipy with vanilla math implementation","description":"# Summary\r\n\r\nHi! This is PR that _mainly_ removes scipy as a dependency. This makes it much easier to carry the package in production reporting environments where either space is limited, or there are complex dependency structures; I deal with this issue a lot.\r\n\r\nAlso, I removed the lockfile ([no reason to commit this in package setting](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/issues/9797#issuecomment-3273767993)). I added pre-commit and lint targets to the makefile which I assume you meant to do.\r\n\r\n# Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I understand and agree to the [Code of Conduct](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/2/1/code_of_conduct/).\r\n- [x] I have followed the [Style Guide for Python Code](https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/) as best as possible for the submitted code.\r\n- [x] I have added **pytest** unit tests for any new functionality.\r\n","published_at":"2026-01-03T19:53:48Z","url":"https://github.com/posit-dev/gt-extras/pull/170","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"tylerriccio33","state":"OPEN"}}
{"source":"github","project_id":"gt-extras","target":"posit-dev/gt-extras","id":"pr/168","ref":168,"title":"chore: bump great tables dev dependency to 0.20.0","description":"This pull request introduces several minor improvements.\r\n\r\n* Introduced a new `pytest.mark.xfail` test for `gt_plt_bar_stack` with a Polars Series, anticipating future support once issue #167 is resolved.\r\n* Updated snapshot tests to reflect updates great-tables 0.20.0 behavior.\r\n* Removed outdated warnings about the package being in development from `README.md` and the introduction article","published_at":"2025-11-03T17:42:24Z","url":"https://github.com/posit-dev/gt-extras/pull/168","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"juleswg23","state":"OPEN"}}
